 228: // The wire anchors are machine names (`seller_sku`, `refforn`); the table shows
 229: // the operator-facing short form. Unknown anchors fall through verbatim — never
 230: // hidden, never renamed into something the wire didn't say.
 231: //
 232: // `refforn` is KEPT even though D-A (D-122) removed it from the cross-side
 233: // anchor vocabulary, so no candidate generated today carries it. D-A also
 234: // decided that already-persisted reasons are NOT migrated, so a decided
 235: // candidate can still hold a `refforn` motivo — audit data that is meant to
 236: // survive verbatim. Dropping the entry would degrade that historical row from
 237: // "Ref. forn." to the raw machine name for no gain.
 238: const anchorShortLabels: Record<string, string> = {
 239:   seller_sku: "SKU",
 240:   ean: "EAN",
 241:   title: "Título",
 242:   marca: "Marca",
 243:   refforn: "Ref. forn.",
 244: };
