Author:     leandrotcawork <leandrotca.work@gmail.com>
AuthorDate: Tue Jul 28 14:33:32 2026 -0300
Commit:     leandrotcawork <leandrotca.work@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Tue Jul 28 14:33:32 2026 -0300

    chip(CHIP-VINC-NEUTRO): fixture-producibility sweep + R-24 correction on the tsc line
    
    Hub precondition before round 5: the "fixture not producible by the wire" class
    had recurred (round 3 claimed it closed, round 4 found two more, one in the file
    round 3 edited) and had no sweep equivalent to the grep-by-STRING that
    discharged the Record-indexed-by-union class.
    
    Swept all 28 candidate fixtures in the write-set against the step that FINALIZES
    a candidate rather than the scoring switch — which was the actual reading error
    behind the recurrence. appendProviderDeclaredUnavailableReasons runs after every
    scoring path and appends one reason per declared anchor with no FOR/AGAINST
    signal, so every candidate of every provider carries a marca reason.
    
    Two findings, both class C, neither reported by any of the four reviewer rounds.
    Both fixtures back criteria: cand_inc (all-INCOMPARABLE) is the V2 deciding
    criterion and cand_noside is V4's honesty rule. Neither is producible for
    mercado_livre, which always emits marca UNAVAILABLE; both are producible for a
    provider that declares marca supplied. Neither fixture was deleted or had marca
    bolted on — that would destroy what each tests. What was wrong was the silence:
    both now state which capability declaration they assume.
    
    V2 also got the producible proof it lacked. New test drives the same defect from
    applyUnresolvedScore's real output for mercado_livre — two INCOMPARABLE/erp
    absences plus marca UNAVAILABLE, the most common row on the screen. Against the
    restored string-literal enumeration it fails with one chip, and the chip that
    survives is "- Marca", the single motivo nothing can be done about, while both
    actionable absences sit behind "+2". The original fixture proves the extreme
    (empty cell) and needs a capability declaration; this proves the common case and
    needs nothing but today's backend.
    
    R-24 correction, made at the source in both artifacts that carried it: the line
    "same 12 as the baseline; this chip neither added nor removed one" was FALSE.
    L0-tsc-baseline.txt has 15 errors including the 3 INCOMPARABLE ones under
    pages/vinculos. The real movement is 15 -> 12 and 3 -> 0: this chip removed 3.
    Caught by the hub's executor seat. The error understated this chip's own
    contribution, which does not make it less false, and it would have made the
    post-merge check read a 15 on integrated main as a regression.
    
    FINDING-7 filed: the golden fixtures are coupled to a backend capability
    declaration by a point-in-time read of Go from TypeScript, with no compiler and
    no test on the seam — same shape as the defect this chip exists to fix, one
    layer up. Recommended to the hub as its own slice; a generator-side JSON dump
    would move it from "a comment claims it" to "the build breaks".
    
    tsc 12 errors, zero under pages/vinculos. vitest 63 files / 525 tests green.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

