================================================================================
A. WIRE DRIFT ON `direction` AND `confidence_band` (Opus rev2 finding #2, extended)
================================================================================

Opus rev2 reported that the drift hardening had been applied to `match_status` ONLY, and that the
V2 fix had made the `direction` path newly REACHABLE: the old compact cell was

    [...byDirection("AGAINST"), ...byDirection("FOR"), ...byDirection("UNAVAILABLE")]

which silently DROPPED a direction it did not enumerate; the total ranking sort that replaced it
keeps every reason. Correct, and the right severity — undoing a silent filter must not install a
literal "undefined" in its place.

A grep-by-STRING over the write-set for the same shape (`Record` indexed by a union, then
deref'd) found a FOURTH site the reviewer did not name: `bandLabels[candidate.confidence_band]`
and `bandClasses[candidate.confidence_band]` at the CONFIANÇA cell. Same defect, same file.

Two tests added, run BEFORE any code change:

    npx --no-install vitest run src/pages/vinculos/QueueTab.test.tsx

    ×  QueueTab > survives a reason direction the SDK union does not know, without printing undefined
       → Unable to find an element with the text: PARTIAL EAN. This could be because the text is
         broken up by multiple elements. [...]

    ×  QueueTab > survives a confidence_band the SDK union does not know, without printing undefined
       → Unable to find an element with the text: CRITICA. This could be because the text is
         broken up by multiple elements. [...]

    Tests  3 failed | 12 passed (15)

The rendered DOM in the second failure carries the defect verbatim — the class attribute ENDS in
the literal string `undefined`:

    <span
      class="inline-flex whitespace-nowrap rounded-full px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-medium undefined"
    />
    <span class="font-mono text-xs font-medium tabular-nums text-muted">
      72%
    </span>

That is an empty pill with a broken class list next to a live confidence number: the operator
reads "72%" with no band at all.

FIX: `directionGlyph` / `directionClass` / `directionRankOf` / `bandLabel` / `bandClass`, each
falling through to the WIRE VALUE verbatim (never to a known member — "–" would read as
UNAVAILABLE and "?" as INCOMPARABLE, which are opposite operator actions) and to a neutral token
pair that asserts none of the semantic readings. The five raw index sites (QueueRow ×4 +
VinculoDrawer ×1) were replaced. The `Record<Union, …>` annotations are UNTOUCHED — they remain
the compile-time guard, per evidence/V-compiletime-guard-still-bites.txt.

Unknown direction ranks 4, after all four known ones, so it can never displace an actionable
signal out of the two compact slots. It is RANKED, not filtered — that is the V2 invariant.

After: 33/33 green in src/pages/vinculos/.

================================================================================
B. `providerDisplayName` INJECTIVITY (Sol rev3 finding #1) AND THE TEST THAT PROVES IT
================================================================================

Sol rev3 refuted the previous fix: the typeset collapsed every separator, so `amazon_marketplace`
and `amazon-marketplace` — both legal, distinct, simultaneously-registrable codes, since
`registry.go` `buildDefinitions` dedupes by exact string equality only — rendered as one
"Amazon Marketplace". Two providers wearing one name is WRONG INFORMATION; a raw slug is merely
ugly. The refutation was accepted.

Sol rev3's SECOND finding was about the test, not the code: the old test asserted a single
hard-coded pair (`shopee` → `Shopee`) and would pass against a fabricated constant fallback.

The strengthened test asserts three codes in one render and that two of them stay DISTINCT. It was
run against BOTH broken implementations Sol named:

--- B.1 against the lossy collapse (the implementation Sol refuted) ---

    return providerCode.split(/[_\-\s]+/).map((w) => (w ? w.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + w.slice(1) : w)).join(" ");

    ×  QueueTab > typesets an unmapped provider without ever collapsing two distinct codes onto one name
       → Unable to find an element with the text: Amazon-marketplace. [...]
          Amazon Marketplace          <-- the collision, on screen
    Tests  1 failed | 14 skipped (15)

--- B.2 against the fabricated constant fallback (the implementation Sol described) ---

    return "Shopee";

    ×  QueueTab > typesets an unmapped provider without ever collapsing two distinct codes onto one name
       → Unable to find an element with the text: Amazon Marketplace. [...]
    Tests  1 failed | 14 skipped (15)

Both probes were reverted from a saved copy of the file; `npx --no-install vitest run
src/pages/vinculos/` came back 33/33 green afterwards, and the shipped body is the round-trip
version.

CORRECTION, recorded because it changed an assertion and not only a comment: the first draft of
this test asserted the hyphenated code would render VERBATIM (`amazon-marketplace`). It renders
`Amazon-marketplace` — `typesetSlug` splits on `_` only, so the hyphen survives, the form
round-trips, and the injectivity check passes it. The two forms are therefore distinct, which is
the property that matters; the assertion was wrong, not the code, and was corrected to the
observed output.

================================================================================
C. GOLDEN FIXTURE PRODUCIBILITY (Opus rev2 findings #1 and #3)
================================================================================

Opus rev2 reported that the fixtures "made honest" in 394c83c were STILL not producible, because
every candidate of every provider carries a `marca` reason the fixtures omit. Verified
independently against the generator, not taken on the reviewer's word:

  - `KnownIdentityAnchors()` is `[seller_sku, ean, title, marca]`
    (connectors/ports/marketplace_capability.go:40-45).
  - `IdentityAnchorAdapter.ProviderIdentityAnchors` walks ALL of them and returns one entry each,
    with `Supplied` set from the provider's declaration (identity_anchor_adapter.go:28-35). The
    list length does not depend on the provider.
  - `mercado_livre` declares `{seller_sku, ean, title}` (mercado_livre/capability_adapter.go:90).
    So `marca` arrives with `Supplied: false`.
  - `appendProviderDeclaredUnavailableReasons` walks `comparison.declared` and emits for every
    anchor with no FOR/AGAINST signal (generation_service.go:671-698). `marca` never has one.
  - `classifyProviderIdentityAnchor` with `!anchor.Supplied` returns
    (UNAVAILABLE, "", "provider não fornece a âncora marca", emit=true) at :700-702.

⇒ EVERY mercado_livre candidate carries `{anchor: "marca", direction: "UNAVAILABLE", detail:
"provider não fornece a âncora marca"}`. The finding is CONFIRMED. Added to all three fixtures.

Consequence, and the reason this was a real defect and not bookkeeping: with three reasons and
COMPACT_CHIP_LIMIT = 2, production renders two chips PLUS a "+1" toggle. The golden was locking a
two-chip cell with no toggle — a layout the backend never produces. The golden now asserts the
toggle (`Mostrar todos os 3 motivos`) and the two-chip cap, i.e. the real layout.

Finding #3, same class, in the same file the previous fix edited and left untouched: both
NO_CANDIDATE fixtures inherited `state: "exact_ean"` from `base()` while carrying
`match_status: "NO_CANDIDATE"` and `reasons: []`. `applyUnresolvedScore` is the only path that
emits NO_CANDIDATE and it is reached through `newCandidate(..., LinkCandidateStateUnresolved,
MatchInputNone, ...)` (generation_service.go:215, :379), and it always seeds two absence reasons
(:620-628). Both fixtures corrected to `state: "unresolved"` with the two INCOMPARABLE/erp
reasons (product is nil on that path ⇒ `missingMatchedAnchorReason` takes the
`product == nil` branch, :631-645) plus `marca`.

Also corrected: that fixture's `provider_code: "xyz-9"`. The reason set depends on the provider's
capability declaration, and there is no declaration in the tree for `xyz-9`, so no reason array
could be claimed producible for it. It is now `mercado_livre`, the one provider with a real
declaration. Nothing was asserted about `xyz-9` in that test; the unmapped-provider path is
covered by name in QueueTab.test.tsx (section B).

